Package: glmseg
Title: Change-Point Detection in Regression Models via the Max-EM Algorithm
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Modibo", "Diabaté", email = "modibo.diabate.pro@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Grégory", "Nuel", role = "aut"),
    person("Olivier", "Bouaziz", role = "aut"))
Description: Detection of an unknown number of change-points in regression
    models using the max-EM algorithm, which combines a constrained hidden
    Markov model with a Classification-EM step. Supports Gaussian (homoscedastic
    and heteroscedastic), logistic, Poisson, and Weibull accelerated failure
    time (survival) regression, with covariates, Fused-Lasso and Binary
    Segmentation initializations, and model selection via BIC (with an optional
    modified penalty to curb over-segmentation). The method is described in
    Diabate, Nuel and Bouaziz (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2025.108278>.
